  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Humanitarian Assistance to crisis-affected populations in Eastern DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">249792</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed Material and Drinking Water for Displaced People and Local Residents</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 21 months intervention&#xA0; intends to provide a rapid relief in the sectors of 1) food and nutrition security, 2) access to basic WASH services and 3) other needs. The main objective of this intervention is to provide a rapid relief for Internally Displaced Persons (IDP) who have lost their goods and livelihoods due to the crisis. It will also intend to support the host communities who often see their livelihoods and living conditions affected by the sudden influx of IDPs. The intervention will target 2 main groups of beneficiairies: one during the first year of intervention (April 2020-January 2021) and the second one during the 2nd year (February -December 2021).</narrative>
  </description>
